Step 4: Post-Patching Steps

Start the database and listener:

sqlplus / as sysdba
SQL> startup;
lsnrctl start

Run datapatch to update SQL components:

cd $ORACLE_HOME/OPatch
./datapatch -verbose

Step 5: Verify Patch Application

Check applied patches:

$ORACLE_HOME/OPatch/opatch lsinventory

Validate SQL patches:

SELECT * FROM dba_registry_sqlpatch;

Best Practices

Always test patches in a non-production environment first.

Ensure all dependent services are stopped before applying patches.

Keep a rollback plan ready by backing up ORACLE_HOME.
